# Keep the build context small. Without this every build ships the whole working
# tree to the daemon — over a gigabyte once a local .venv exists, against ~50 MB
# of actual source.
#
# The exception is the git ref metadata: docker/server/carbonteq/version.sh
# resolves HEAD from it to derive the release version, so a build needs no
# manually supplied version. Only the refs are kept, not .git/objects, which is
# the bulk of it — see version.sh for how it reads them without a git binary.

.git
!.git/HEAD
!.git/refs
!.git/packed-refs

.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/node_modules
